<section id="kmeans-as-a-vector-quantization-1" class="slide level2">
<h2>Kmeans As A Vector Quantization</h2>
<h3 id="problem-setting">Problem Setting</h3>
<div class="fragment" style="margin-top: 30px; font-size: 0.6em;">
<ul>
<li><strong>Compression loss:</strong> <span class="math inline">\ell(\mathbf{x}_i, c_k) = \|\mathbf{x}_i - c_k\|^2 = \sum_{j=1}^d (x_{ij} - c_{kj})^2</span></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="fragment" style="font-size: 0.6em; margin-top: 20px; ">
<ul>
<li><p>A <strong><span class="math inline">K</span>-point quantizer</strong> associated with codebook <span class="math inline">\mathcal{C}</span> is any mapping: <span class="math display">q : \mathbb{R}^d \to \mathcal{C} = \{c_k : k = 1, \ldots, K\}</span> <span class="math display">\mathbf{x}_i \mapsto q(\mathbf{x}_i) = c_k \text{ for some } k.</span></p></li>
<li><p>We define <span style="color:red;"><strong>Within Sum of Square</strong></span> criterion for a quantizer <span class="math inline">q</span> by: <span class="math display">\text{WSS}(q) = \sum_{i=1}^n \ell(\mathbf{x}_i, q(\mathbf{x}_i)) = \sum_{i=1}^n \|\mathbf{x}_i - q(\mathbf{x}_i)\|^2</span></p></li>
<li><p><span style="color:#4472C4;"><strong>Objective:</strong></span> find <span class="math inline">q^*</span> that provides the lowest <span style="color:red;"><strong>WSS</strong></span>, i.e., <span class="math display">\text{WSS}(q^*) = \min_{q \in \mathcal{Q}} \text{WSS}(q)</span></p></li>
</ul>
